.TH TRAFIX 1 "May 2026" "0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trafix \- Lightweight network monitoring tool for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trafix
.RI [ OPTION ]
.br
.B trafix interfaces
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B trafix connections
.RI [ --json ]
.RI [ "--proto tcp|udp" ]
.RI [ "--state STATE" ]
.br
.B trafix listeners
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B trafix system
.RI [ --json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Trafix is a lightweight terminal user interface and scriptable command-line tool that provides insights into Linux system, connection, and network activity.

Running
.B trafix
without options launches the interactive TUI.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B interfaces
Print current network interface byte counters. Text output is the default; use
.B --json
for JSON output.
.TP
.B connections
Print current TCP/UDP connections. Text output is the default; use
.B --json
for JSON output.
.TP
.B listeners
Print local listening sockets. Text output is the default; use
.B --json
for JSON output.
.TP
.B system
Print a compact system overview. Text output is the default; use
.B --json
for JSON output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Display this help message and exit.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B --json
Use JSON output for scriptable commands.
.TP
.BI "--proto " tcp|udp
Filter
.B connections
output by protocol.
.TP
.BI "--state " STATE
Filter
.B connections
output by connection state, such as
.B ESTABLISHED
or
.BR LISTEN .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments or general command failure.
.TP
.B 2
Required collector data is unavailable or permission-limited.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Masoud Bolhassani.
